WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.965 --> 00:00:06.320
Speaker 1: Another thing that is haunting&nbsp;
the Democrats ahead of the 2022 midterms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:13.280
Joe Biden's approval rating has taken another&nbsp;
major hit, this time among young voters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:19.520
those aged 18 to 30, according to the&nbsp;
latest round of polling out there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:26.640
Joe Biden now has a net negative 23 percent&nbsp;
approval rating with that particular age group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:33.680
that, for the record, helped push him past Donald&nbsp;
Trump in the 2020 election. His disapproval&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.320
rating with that age group right now is 50&nbsp;
percent approval rating. With that age group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.840
is 27 percent. That's where you get the twenty&nbsp;
three net difference between the two numbers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.400
And that, again, is going to hurt Joe&nbsp;
Biden in the midterms and of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.240
the Democratic Party, since Joe Biden is clearly&nbsp;
not on the ballot there. But that age group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:02.240
which does now, you know, when you take the&nbsp;
millennials and the other age groups, they make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.240
up one of the largest voting blocs in the country.&nbsp;
They are the largest voting bloc in the country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.840
So when they're looking at this administration&nbsp;
after putting you in office just a year ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.400
and they're saying we're not happy with what&nbsp;
you're giving us because what you're giving us is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.960
effectively nothing, then that's a big problem for&nbsp;
the Democratic Party that they're going to have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.840
find a way to overcome prior to those midterms.&nbsp;
One of the things obviously driving factor in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.720
this decision to no longer support Joe Biden&nbsp;
with his age group is the student loan debt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:38.800
Biden specifically promised. And you can still go&nbsp;
back on his Twitter feed and see where he promised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:46.800
$10000 student loan debt forgiveness, at&nbsp;
the very least $10000. And it's not there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:53.120
Oh, sure, he is forgiven debt for some people.&nbsp;
But you've got to jump through so many hoops in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:58.240
order to qualify for the debt that has been&nbsp;
forgiven so far that it effectively amounts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.800
to what one percent maybe of total debt held.&nbsp;
I think it's actually lower than one percent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.760
No, that's not good enough, you're not&nbsp;
going to win back over this age group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.000
that is saddled with one and a half&nbsp;
trillion dollars of student loan debt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:21.280
With a one percent forgiveness for some people who&nbsp;
meet all of these, you know, very strict criteria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.680
not happening. And for the record, student&nbsp;
loan debt does not just affect that generation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.960
You have people in their 60s in this&nbsp;
country that still have student loan debt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:35.840
You know, obviously a lot of that is because&nbsp;
these people went to college late in their lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.200
But they're still paying this off. This is an&nbsp;
issue that does affect every generation here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.920
in the United States. It is not just&nbsp;
the young voters, but specifically he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.840
promised them. He told them again, it's still&nbsp;
on Twitter. You can go and see it for yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:57.680
And he hasn't done it. And that's something&nbsp;
that he could do via executive order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.880
now, for the record, too. There's a lot of&nbsp;
people out there who say, no, he can't do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.200
it via executive order. A lot of people who&nbsp;
says, yes, he can do it via executive order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.360
And the discrepancy between the two is has to&nbsp;
do with the public student loan debt and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.920
private student loan debt. Meaning if you took out&nbsp;
your federal loans, you know you did your FAFSA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.840
and you got your student loans from the federal&nbsp;
government itself, you know, the Department of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.640
Education. That's what Biden could forgive&nbsp;
now if you took out separate student loans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:32.400
because banks do offer those that would probably&nbsp;
take an act of legislation. Right. I know I had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.880
couple myself. The interest rates on those were&nbsp;
absolutely astronomical, but luckily for me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.440
the amounts I took out from private banks&nbsp;
were so small I was able to pay them off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:47.040
you know, within a 10 year period. Not, not&nbsp;
quickly, obviously, but those I did work to pay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:52.160
off first because I really couldn't get deferment&nbsp;
on those either. And that actually, unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.200
is a lot of the problem. Those private student&nbsp;
loan debts, the ones with the higher interest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:03.840
rates, the ones with the stricter criteria in&nbsp;
order to get deferments and forbearance. So that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.600
does take an act of legislation. But Biden could&nbsp;
for this age group at the very least, give this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:14.640
executive order. Show them he's doing something,&nbsp;
show them. He understands their concerns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:21.600
for the future. Throw them a bone here. And it&nbsp;
may just help to save Democrats in the midterms,

